From: arcade-runtime-ts
Subject: [PATCH] devfind: keep ioport_array_finder tags alive

ioport_array_finder built each tag with strformat() and handed the
finder the c_str() of the returned temporary copy, which is destroyed at
the end of the statement. Natively the freed buffer usually still holds
the text, so the lookup works by accident; under the Emscripten
allocator it is reused at once and every port found through a basetag
array (for example the segaorun.c ADC ports) resolves to NULL, so
read_safe() returns its default and the analogue inputs never reach the
game. Format into the member string first and pass its own buffer.

--- a/src/emu/devfind.h
+++ b/src/emu/devfind.h
@@ -268,7 +268,9 @@
 	ioport_array_finder(device_t &base, const char *basetag)
 	{
 		for (int index = 0; index < _Count; index++) {
-			m_array[index].reset(global_alloc(ioport_finder_type(base, strformat(m_tag[index], "%s.%d", basetag, index).c_str())));
+			// strformat returns a copy; taking c_str() of that temporary left the finder with a dangling tag pointer
+			strformat(m_tag[index], "%s.%d", basetag, index);
+			m_array[index].reset(global_alloc(ioport_finder_type(base, m_tag[index].c_str())));
 		}
 	}
 
